   "answer": "FOODS_3 on 2013-12-25 (Christmas Day) \u2014 the largest single-day absolute error in the whole backtest, 2,431.5 units. The store was closed: actual sales were 0 units, but the model forecast 2,431.5. The seasonal-naive baseline made the same mistake, though smaller (1,755 units predicted, i.e. 1,755 units of error). Christmas Day is in fact the worst day for six of the seven departments (FOODS_3 646.9\u2192 no: HOUSEHOLD_1 646.9, HOBBIES_1 481.3, FOODS_2 382.2, HOUSEHOLD_2 159.9 units of error; FOODS_1's worst was 2013-12-21 at 326.4 units, with 12-25 second at 298.6; only HOBBIES_2 differs, worst on 2013-09-08 at 50.4 units). FOODS_3 tops the list simply because it is by far the largest department (615,655 units over the window). Nothing anomalous about demand happened \u2014 this is a closed-store zero-sales day that neither the model nor the baseline encodes.",
